+- 最終画像：PNG／RGB／1600 × 900 px。Pillowで再度開いて全画素を読み込み、形式・モード・寸法・ファイルの存在を確認。
+- やり直した回数：1回（初回生成を除くimage_genによる修正。寸法調整は含めない）。
+- 目視確認：文字・数字・ロゴ・透かし・記号列の混入なし。概念図としての輪郭、矢印、器械の構造を確認。
+- 初稿では標的付近に不完全な短い格子線があり、三脚の足元も切れていたため修正。最終画像では直交格子、標的の点、方向と距離を表す矢印、全体が収まった三脚、画面内の抽象的な3本のバーを確認。点と格子の位置関係は模式表現であり、画素位置から座標を読み取る図ではない。
+
+### 使用したプロンプト
+
+```text
+Use case: scientific-educational.
+Create one calm precise textbook plate illustrating how a total station's observed direction and distance determine a coordinate point.
+Canvas: landscape 16:9, approximately 1600 x 900 pixels, opaque RGB PNG.
+Style: flat tidy conceptual illustration with crisp navy #1F4E79 outlines, teal #13877B direction accents and burnt-orange #BD512B distance accents, uniform warm ivory #FAF9F5 background. Limited colors, generous margins. No photorealism or dramatic shadows.
+Composition: a simplified generic total station mounted correctly on a tripod occupies the left quarter. Three distinct legs join a single leveling base. A small telescope between two supports points toward the right; a visible small rectangular instrument screen contains ONLY three solid abstract horizontal bars of different lengths, with absolutely no numerals, letters, ticks or button symbols.
+On the right half draw a sparse flat orthogonal coordinate grid, shown face-on as evenly spaced horizontal and vertical thin pale navy lines, without axes labels or tick labels. Highlight one intersection in the upper-right part of this grid with a prominent filled teal circular point. The point must lie exactly on the crossing of one vertical and one horizontal grid line.
+A single straight navy sight line with a teal arrowhead runs diagonally upward from the telescope toward this exact highlighted grid intersection. Beside and parallel to the sight line draw a slim orange double-headed arrow denoting measured distance. Near the instrument, a short faint horizontal reference ray and one small teal angular arc between this ray and the sight line denote observed direction. Make the angle's vertex align with the telescope/sight-line origin. The direction line and the distance arrow visually converge on the same target point. No additional unrelated dots.
+This is a conceptual transition from instrument observations to a coordinate point, not a realistic scene. Keep geometric construction clean and uncluttered. No people, landscape, real branded products, equations, legends, decorative marks, or strings of symbols.
+Strict exclusions: no text, no numbers, no letters, no logos, no watermark.
+```
+
+### 修正プロンプト
+
+直前に生成した当該画像1枚を編集対象として使用（`num_last_images_to_include: 1`）。
+
+```text
+Revise this total-station coordinate textbook illustration, retaining the warm ivory background and limited navy, teal, orange palette, wide 16:9 composition, total station at left, observed direction and distance arrows, and orthogonal grid at right. no text, no numbers, no letters, no logos, no watermark.
+Correct two construction details:
+1. The coordinate grid must consist solely of complete evenly spaced straight horizontal and vertical grid lines. Remove the stray short horizontal line through the teal target. Relocate the teal target dot onto the existing complete grid intersection one row LOWER than the top horizontal grid line, on the same vertical grid line as before. Both the navy sight-line arrow and the parallel orange double-headed distance arrow must adjust naturally toward this revised target. No partial extra grid lines or off-grid points.
+2. Reduce the instrument and tripod silhouette slightly so that all three tripod feet are fully visible with clear ivory margin below, not cropped or cut off. Use an especially simple flat silhouette, no shadow or photorealistic detail. Keep the visible screen with only three solid horizontal bars.
+Preserve a clean small teal angular arc between the horizontal reference ray and the navy sight line, centered on their common origin at the telescope. No extra diagrams or labels.
+```
+
+## 講義での使用上の区別
+
+3枚とも概念を伝えるための挿絵であり、実測図・観測データ・数値計算用の作図ではない。角度や距離、座標値は画像から読み取らない。
+

